What c1205469 does:
• `maxTurns` now applies. When the agent tool builds a child for a definition, it sets the definition's turn cap after the shared default of 25, so the file's value wins. A file without maxTurns keeps 25; the commit body says that default is yoyo's choice, not Claude Code's. When a child hits its cap, yoagent's existing stop notice tells the parent the answer is partial. No turn counter or "partial" marker of yoyo's own was added.
• Bad values are skipped with a reason. maxTurns: 0 used to load, because the old check only rejected negative numbers; it is now skipped with a reason. Negative numbers, non-integers and strings were already skipped, and now have pinned tests. Large values are used as written.
• `yoyo agents` no longer misleads. The header no longer says "not yet used by yoyo", which had been false since 40028335 (#1252). Each row's model: X now carries "(not honoured yet: runs on sub_agent_model, else the main model)", which matches how yoyo picks the sub-agent's model.
• Docs: docs/src/usage/commands.md, ARCHITECTURE.md and the comments in agent_dispatch.rs say maxTurns is honoured and model is not yet.

The commit body says yoagent's sub-agent tool has no way to read back its turn cap, so the test checks the value a small helper passes through on the build path. This run did not repeat the positive control (break the cap call, watch the test fail, restore). src/agent_dispatch.rs is now 758 lines, past the ~700 you flagged; the file-size test passed as part of cargo test.

